# A game against the computer (Easy, playing White): a move, Submit, the computer's reply, and the "thinking" HUD.
# Layout (1400x800): Versus (150,250), Computer (833,122), Easy (644,226), Standard (690,320), Play (808,712), Submit (841,90).
# `ainodes` pins how far the computer's search gets each frame: the capture of the indicator is taken with the search frozen
# part-way (the bar at what the search has done so far), and `waitai` runs frames until it has replied.
wait 20
click 150 250        # Versus
wait 30
click 833 122        # Computer
wait 20
click 644 226        # Easy (White is the default side)
wait 10
click 690 320        # Standard
wait 20
click 808 712        # Play
wait 120
capture vs-game-start
clicksq 0 0 e2
wait 40
clicksq 0 0 e4
wait 40
ainodes 1            # a very slow search ...
click 841 90         # Submit
wait 20
ainodes 0            # ... frozen where it is
wait 5
capture vs-thinking              # "Computer is thinking" with the progress bar; Submit and Undo are not offered
clicksq 0 1 e7       # the computer's pawn: the boards ignore the click during its turn
wait 40
capture vs-thinking-input-blocked
ainodes 400
waitai               # the computer plays its reply and the legal-turn search of the game finishes
wait 90
capture vs-game-computer-replied   # White to move again, the computer's reply on the board
clicksq 0 2 g1
wait 40
capture vs-game-knight-selected    # the player is in control again
